@h1 Headings & structure h1@

Six heading levels give a document its outline:

@@@pre
@h1 The Lamp Keeper h1@
@h2 Chapter One h2@
@h3 The Arrival h3@
pre@@@

@h2 Sectioning h2@

For a longer document, semantic wrappers mirror the shape of the page:

@ul
@li @code section code@, @code article code@ — major divisions li@
@li @code header code@, @code footer code@ — a section's top and tail li@
@li @code aside code@, @code nav code@, @code main code@ — supporting regions li@
ul@

@@@pre
@article
  @header @h1 A Report h1@ header@
  @section
    Body prose…
  section@
article@
pre@@@

These are optional. Reach for them when the structure helps a reader (or a
screen reader); skip them when plain headings are enough.
